> API and interpretation

Fractions are truncated, never rounded, and the point is retained at zero
requested fractional digits. Zero radicand gives requested zeros. Negative
counts fail before computation; complete digit and copied-history character
policies are explicit. Correctness is checked with exact integer inequalities or
integer square roots, since a parsed double cannot certify arbitrarily many
decimal digits.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

